# AstroTag QA & Persona Protocol

Before finalizing **any major feature, feed change, or economic update**, mentally simulate **both tiers** (see `docs/QA_PERSONA_PROTOCOL.md`).

## Two tiers (non-negotiable)

| Tier | Identity | Freedom | Discipline |
|------|----------|---------|------------|
| **User** | `profiles` — organic members | Post, like, reply; optional `profiles.avatar_url` | Context tag required; 3 posts/day; 100 likes/day (Istanbul); moderation on all text |
| **Expert** | `expert_profiles` — verified providers | Vitrin, announcements, service cards, crystal economy | `expert_profiles.avatar_url` required for new services & announcements; **no** commercial spam in feed |

## Pre-ship checklist (feed / social)

- [ ] `user_post` blocked without valid `context_tag` (`feed-context-tags.shared.ts`)
- [ ] `moderateFeedText` runs server-side on posts, captions, replies (`feed-moderation.shared.ts`)
- [ ] User daily caps enforced in server actions, not UI-only (`feed-rate-limit.server.ts`)
- [ ] Expert avatar guard on service **create** & feed announcements (`expert-avatar-guard.server.ts`)
- [ ] Sales/commerce only via approved **expert service cards** — never free-form feed CTAs
- [ ] Red-heart like UX preserved for emotional engagement; compact noir/zinc UI not regressed

## Pre-ship checklist (expert economy)

- [ ] Crystal spend / commission paths unchanged unless explicitly scoped
- [ ] RLS + service-role validation remain defense-in-depth for feed inserts

When proposing architecture, state which personas pass/fail and which tier a change favors.
